    "case_study": "May 2024 Gannon / Mother's Day solar storm",
    "record_count": 14,
    "measurement_notes": [
      "Solar flare start, peak, end, class, active region and location are event metadata transcribed from the NASA CCMC DONKI weekly summary.",
      "Proton flux values are integral GOES proton flux in pfu, where 1 pfu = 1 proton/(cm^2 s sr).",
      "The >10 MeV peaks of 208 pfu (2024-05-10 17:45 UTC) and 116 pfu (2024-05-11 09:10 UTC) are reported by the cited 2026 research article; they are not reconstructed from raw five-minute samples in this file.",
      "NASA CCMC event report gives the GOES >10 MeV threshold-crossing times for SEP episodes; it does not give every episode's peak flux.",
      "The >100 MeV peak is described by the NASA technical presentation as just over 7 pfu; it is not entered as an exact numeric value in the structured flux field.",
      "Blank proton flux fields mean the cited source did not provide a numerical peak; they do not mean zero flux.",
      "Flare-to-SEP associations are reported associations, not proof that a single flare alone caused the full particle event."
    ],
